{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "WS2811",
 "kind": "led_driver",
 "manufacturer": "Worldsemi",
 "title": "WS2811: three-channel 256-level constant-current LED driver with single-wire cascaded data",
 "source": {
  "revision": "V1.1, 2017-10-09",
  "pages": 8
 },
 "summary": "An eight-pin driver for one RGB light point: three outputs each sink a fixed 16.5 mA typ and are dimmed by 8-bit PWM (256 levels, scan rate above 2 kHz), and the outputs tolerate 12 V. Colour data arrives on one wire as an NRZ pulse-width code at 800 kbps; each chip keeps the first 24 bits it sees, regenerates the rest and sends them out of DO to the next chip, so chips chain without the edges degrading. An internal regulator lets the chip run from a rail up to 24 V through one series resistor on VDD. It comes in SOP8 and MSOP8.",
